          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its later characterization as false bears on sincerity, not on its clear avowal form and force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Je vous aime! — сказал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"later_1\",\"quotation\":\"когда он сказал эти невыходившие из него слова: «Je vous aime»\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.82,\"reason\":\"In this represented situation, Pierre uses the avowal as the expected romantic formula completing or ratifying his already socially established engagement to Hélène. It therefore invokes their prospective marital relationship, but it is not itself an explicit proposal or promise: the narration already calls her his fiancée before he speaks.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The utterance is not represented as a reflexive or eruptive discharge of affect. Pierre pauses, searches for the conventionally appropriate words, and deliberately recalls them; their delivery is notably inadequate rather than spontaneous.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтò такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love and weakly ratifying the relationship, the expression functions as compliance with a socially expected romantic script. Pierre says what he believes one is required to say in such circumstances, amid strong social pressure toward the marriage.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after her family has already treated them as engaged. Following physical intimacy and while holding his fiancée's hand, Pierre recalls and utters the expected declaration of love, which sounds poor and embarrasses him.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Pierre weakly ratifies or invokes the prospective marital relationship already imposed and acknowledged by the surrounding company; the target does not independently state a proposal or specify marital obligations. Hélène's immediate physical intimacy supplies nonverbal uptake, and the supplied text says they marry a month and a half later. At the moment Pierre thinks that he loves her, but his later reflection calls the declaration a lie and says he never loved her.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"I recognise the supplied passage as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace; the classification relies only on the supplied blocks.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence strongly establishes the avowal's conventional force but gives conflicting evidence about genuine love: Pierre internally tells himself he loves Hélène at the moment, while later judging the words false. Hélène gives no verbal response to the target, and the precise commitment attributable to this sentence alone remains limited because the engagement has effectively been established before it is spoken.\"}"
        }
